Chapter: ProbeClosureBasecase

 Finding 38 says the fault needs a self tail call to be EXECUTED. This
 asks whether it needs one at all, or only needs the definition to
 contain one.

 `count-down 0` takes the base case immediately: the recursive arm is
 never entered, so no jump to loop-top ever happens, but the definition
 still contains a self tail call and so is still compiled with TCO
 active. Finding 38's own reproducer only ever called `count-down 3`.

 `basecase 47` means the tail call must actually run, and finding 38's
 headline stands. A fault means the defect is about a function-returning
 definition being compiled with TCO active at all, the executed jump is
 incidental, and the headline is wrong.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  count-down : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  count-down (n) = if n == 0 then add3 5 else count-down (n - 1)

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("basecase " & show (((count-down 0) 20) 22))
  end
